  <running_head>De Duellis.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>que</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">veterato, ne nimium grassare-</l>
    <l n="2">tur, maximo reipublicæ dam-</l>
    <l n="3">no. Et erat cum cautelâ, per-</l>
    <l n="4">mittendum, quod propter hu-</l>
    <l n="5">mani generis duritiem auferri</l>
    <l n="6">non poterat, nisi ab eo, qui</l>
    <l n="7">summâ in Imperio gauderet</l>
    <l n="8">potestate. Hinc ita restringe-</l>
    <l n="9">bantur congressus singulares,</l>
    <l n="10">ne cuiquam privatoidque pro-</l>
    <l n="11">priâ auctoritate, eos indicere,</l>
    <l n="12">aut suscipere liceret. Secus si</l>
    <l n="13">factum esset, partes incurre-</l>
    <l n="14">bant homicidii crimen, &amp;</l>
    <l n="15">quod longè maximum est,</l>
    <l n="16">Majestatis. Solus itaque Prin-</l>
    <l n="17">ceps in Galliâ hodie permittit</l>
    <l n="18">illa duella, licet raro. Olim</l>
    <l n="19">etiam causa cognita, Senatus</l>
    <l n="20">Parisiensis. Curia itidem gu-</l>
    <l n="21">bernatoris, cum ipso rectore</l>
    <l n="22">Delphinatus in Delphinatu:</l>
    <l n="23">Magister militum Galliæ, seu</l>
    <l n="24">connestabulus. Reguli Italiæ</l>
    <l n="25">passim sine delectu non tantum</l>
    <l n="26">permittebant, sed insuper quo-</l>
    <l n="27">que</l>
  </main_text>
